    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Grimes Clontarf are thrilled to bring 2 Kincora Avenue to the market. This well-maintained red brick family home is ideally located on Kincora Avenue on one of the most sought-after roads in Clontarf. This is a wonderful opportunity to acquire a fantastic family home in a much sought-after area of Clontarf. This property will allow a discerning purchaser to put their own stamp on this lovely home.\r\n\r\nNo. 2 is a deceptively spacious family home measuring approx. 133 sq m /  1,431 sq ft. Internally the property is well laid out and there is a wonderful sense of space as one walks through the house. The accommodation briefly comprises entrance hall, two reception rooms, shower room, kitchen / breakfast room and utility room all located downstairs. While upstairs there are 2 large double bedrooms, a single bedroom, WC and bathroom. The private rear garden has side access and is laid in lawn with mature planting and to the front is a driveway with off-street parking and a walled garden.\r\n \r\nSituated on Kincora Avenue, a mature and settled area, the location is second to none. Clontarf Promenade and cycle track are approximately a 5-minute walk, while Clontarf Village with its excellent selection of restaurants and boutiques is also within walking distance. The area is well- serviced by public transport - the 130 bus route has stops in close proximity providing easy access to the City Centre. In addition to this, there are an abundance of excellent schools and sporting facilities in the immediate vicinity as well as St. Anne’s Park and Dollymount Strand."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall:\r\nBright and spacious hall accessed via a storm porch\r\n\r\nReception Room 1 / Dining Room:\r\nLarge bright room to the front of the house with laminate flooring and open fireplace with marble surround and double doors to:\r\n\r\nReception Room 2 / Living Room\r\nLocated to rear of the house overlooking the garden with a recently installed multi fuel stove with marble surround, laminate flooring and patio doors to rear\r\n\r\nShower Room:\r\nFully tiled with WC, heated towel rail, wash hand basin with storage and walk-in rain head shower\r\n\r\nKitchen / Breakfast Room:\r\nFitted with wall and floor units. Single oven, hob and extractor fan, fridge / freezer and dishwasher. Ample dining space and access to covered side passage and outside WC\r\n\r\nWC:\r\nWC and wash hand basin\r\n\r\nUtility Room:\r\nPlumbed for washer and drier with built-in shelving\r\n\r\nBedroom 1:\r\nLarge double bedroom to rear of the house with carpet flooring and built-in wardrobes\r\n\r\nBedroom 2:\r\nLarge double bedroom to the front of the property with carpet flooring and built-in wardrobes\r\n\r\nBedroom 3:\r\nSingle bedroom to the front of the house with built-in wardrobe and carpet flooring\r\n\r\nWC:\r\nFully tiled with WC\r\n\r\nBathroom:\r\nFully tiled with wash hand basin with storage and bath with shower attachment\r\n\r\nAttic:\r\nFully insulated storage attic\r\n\r\nOutside:\r\nThe private split level rear garden is laid predominantly in lawn with mature planting and storage sheds and has a covered side passage. While to the front is a driveway with off-street parking and a walled garden.\r\n\r\nServices:\r\nGas Fired Central Heating\r\nDriveway with off-street parking to the front\r\nAlarm Panel\r\nNew Rationel windows\r\n\r\nBER Details:\r\nBER: C\r\nBER No. 114335326\r\n\r\nContents:\r\nCarpets, curtains, blinds, light fittings, fixtures and fittings\r\nIntegrated and non-integrated appliances"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Charming 3 bed semi-detached family home \r\nApprox. 133 sq m / 1,431 sq ft \r\nConvenient and highly sought-after location\r\nLocated minutes’ walk from Clontarf Promenade\r\nLovingly cared for family home"
      },
